gorgias-polus.logic.r1: argue/equivocates: C (S32): "evil" is taken as is worse for the doer than suffering wrong is for the victim, the sense of Polus's "more evil" in S18 that S32/S36 claim to refute in C and as exceeds in harm or badness as the standard of disgrace (S11, S20), harm done by the act, not necessarily to the doer where dw_more_evil is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S32) does not follow (gorgias-polus.logic.r1.sense1)
gorgias-polus.logic.r1: argue/countermodel: C (S32): dw_more_disgraceful = T, dw_more_evil = T, dw_more_evil_2 = F, dw_more_pain = F
